<Base title="About Me | The Founder Edit" current="about">
  <article class="about"><h1>About Me</h1><p class="lede">Publishing my entrepreneurship journey to share some of my most heartfelt experiences.</p><h2>My Story</h2><p>Hi! I'm Wen. I'm a Malaysian born and bred in Klang — thoroughbred, as both my parents were born in Klang too. Youngest of four girls in our family, I was super spoilt growing up! I have the best sisters anyone could ever ask for, and my mom, who is also my partner in crime!</p><p>Fairly independent, I think. Haha. For the last ten years I've run SushiVid, an influencer marketing platform serving Malaysia and Singapore — through the golden years, a boycott, a downsizing, and an AI reinvention. The team that remains is my extended family, and I love them to bits. Somewhere along the way I also picked up a jewellery brand, a creative space, a Shopee store, and a court case's worth of stories. I write about all of it here.</p><p>In my free time, I love to be outdoors — lazing by the pool is my current favourite. You can also find me snuggled up with a hot cocoa at a cafe with my head planted in my book.</p><h2>What I'm Building</h2><p>One company was never going to be enough for me — I've come to accept that building is simply how I'm wired. When I decide to start something, I just start. Here's the honest portfolio, and each one has its own story on this blog.</p><div class="ventures"><a class="venture" href="https://sushivid.com/?utm_source=yuhwen&utm_medium=blog&utm_campaign=about" rel="noopener"><span class="v-name">SushiVid</span><span class="v-desc">My first and longest love. Ten years of connecting brands with creators across Malaysia &amp; Singapore — through the golden years, the hard years, and now an AI-powered reinvention. "The transparent influencer marketplace" isn't a slogan; I went to court to keep it true. Half this blog is really SushiVid's story.</span><span class="v-link">sushivid.com →</span></a><a class="venture" href="https://thousandgold.co/?utm_source=yuhwen&utm_medium=blog&utm_campaign=about" rel="noopener"><span class="v-name">Yù · ThousandGold</span><span class="v-desc">The feminine comeback. I'm one of four sisters who all share the middle name Yù — jade — and this jewellery brand is named for us. Every piece documents a family memory: an open diary, written in gold. Started at 40, first sold at bazaars, where my handmade pieces kept selling out faster than I could make them.</span><span class="v-link">thousandgold.co →</span></a><a class="venture" href="https://socialantisocialsociety.com/?utm_source=yuhwen&utm_medium=blog&utm_campaign=about" rel="noopener"><span class="v-name">Social Anti Social Society</span><span class="v-desc">A cozy creative and workshop space made for introverts — because some of us recharge best in quiet company. Born from the same instinct as everything else I build: make the thing you wish existed.</span><span class="v-link">socialantisocialsociety.com →</span></a><a class="venture" href="https://my.shp.ee/TiPUDp6v" rel="noopener"><span class="v-name">Pegawai Gudang</span><span class="v-desc">The unglamorous one — and surprisingly good business. A Shopee treasure hunt of clearance finds, born when friends' warehouses overflowed after COVID. Also home of PG-18, our plus-size menswear basics, inspired by someone dear to me who deserved better options in his size.</span><span class="v-link">on Shopee →</span></a></div><h2>Greatest Moment In Life</h2><p>My favourite holidays are often in the snow! I would play anything from snowboards to sleds. One of my greatest memories in life was when I soaked in a natural hot spring with some friends while watching a meteor shower. Definitely one of the best moments of my life.</p><h2>Favourite Book</h2><p>I have so many books I love, but my favourites are autobiographies — and if I absolutely have to pick one, I loved the Steve Jobs biography by Walter Isaacson. I read it while I was in Bali, in 2013. It was my first introduction to the tech world.</p><h2>Most Embarrassing Moment</h2><p>The most embarrassing moment of my life was when I was posing on stage for a small modelling gig. I was so very nervous that day that when I smiled, my face was involuntarily twitching. I couldn't make it stop! Anyone else who has experienced this — do you know a solution to my twitchy smile?</p></article>
</Base>

